# === Claude workflow kit — not versioned ===
# The kit is personal tooling, maintained upstream, not a deliverable of this
# project. It stays on disk and keeps working — the hooks, the rules and the
# commands are read from the filesystem, not from Git.
#
# What that costs, so nobody rediscovers it the hard way: a fresh clone has NO
# guardrails. No TDD freeze, no architecture hook, no CLAUDE.md, no rules. The
# CI is then the only enforcement that survives cloning, which is precisely why
# `.github/workflows/` stays versioned.
#
# These paths were tracked by the bootstrap commit, so they were also detached
# with `git rm --cached`: an ignore rule alone never stops Git following what it
# already follows.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
workflow.py
workflow.sh
codex-handoff.sh
docs/Claude_Workflows.md
docs/ADAPTATION.md
docs/research-cache/

# src/routeTree.gen.ts is deliberately NOT ignored, though TanStack Router
# generates it. `pnpm build` is `tsc --noEmit && vite build`, and only the
# second half writes that file: ignored, the CI typechecks a tree where it does
# not exist yet and fails before ever building.
